
# Lab Experiment 2
## Refactor to Engineering-Grade HTML (M1)

### Project Title
Hospital Patient Appointment Management Website

### Objective
To refactor a non-semantic HTML webpage
using HTML5 semantic elements and improve
accessibility of the patient appointment form.

### Technologies Used
- HTML5
- CSS3
- Visual Studio Code
- Git and GitHub

### Semantic Elements Used
- header
- nav
- main
- section
- article
- aside
- footer

### Accessibility Improvements
- Proper heading hierarchy
- Labels for all form fields
- Correct input types
- Required field validation
- Telephone number pattern validation
- Keyboard navigation
- Visible focus indicators
- Screen reader landmarks

### Testing Tools
- Google Lighthouse
- WAVE Accessibility Checker
- Windows Narrator

### Accessibility Audit

| Metric | Before | After |
|---|---|---|
| Semantic Structure | Poor | Improved |
| Form Labels | Missing | Added |
| Input Validation | Missing | Implemented |
| Keyboard Access | Limited | Improved |
| Screen Reader | Poor | Improved |

